  "query_preview": "..\nAn upper low over central-southern California will continue to\nbring southwesterly flow across the region. Tucson's PWATs are\ncurrently 0.89 inches from GOES and moisture content will \nincrease through the rest of the day. Majority of the moisture \nwill be in the form of cloud but there are slight chances for \nshower and thunderstorms from Tucson and east. \n\nThe upper level low over central-southern California will\ncontinue to bring moisture for the next 3 days. The bulk of the\nmoisture will be sitting to our east and Tucson will be on the \nouter edge of above normal moisture. There will be daily chances\nfor rain showers and thunderstorms through Thursday. Latest CAM\nguidance has showers starting late tonight and increasing \ncoverage by tomorrow afternoon. There are 10% from Sells to 50% \nby the New Mexico state line for a quarter of inch of rain in a\n6 hour period. Chances for half inch are 10-40% in a 6 hour \nperiod will be along the state line. Rain and thunderstorm \nchances will continue through Thursday. \n\nBy Friday, upper level moisture will decrease and as result,\nlower chances for rain showers and thunderstorms. Daily chances\nwill return by Sunday, but there are still disagreement on how \nthe ensembles try to resolve the influence of Tropical Storm \nPolo. For now, rain and thunderstorm chances will be 25-30% for \nthe start of the new week.",
